## Statistical test

### Chirality
```{r}
set.seed(42)
adonis2(
  PC_scores ~ Chirality,
  data = data_combined,
  method = "euclidean",
  permutations = 9999,
)
```
PERMANOVA showed a significant difference in shape  between sinistral and dextral. 

### interaction between Chirality and Region
```{r}
set.seed(42)
adonis2(
  PC_scores ~ Region * Chirality,
  data = data_combined,
  method = "euclidean",
  by = "terms",
  permutations = 9999
)
```
### Region
#### Sinistral
```{r}
set.seed(42)
adonis_Sinistral <- adonis2(
  PC_scores[specimen_info_matched$Chirality == "Sinistral", ] ~ Region,
  data = data_combined[specimen_info_matched$Chirality == "Sinistral", ],
  method = "euclidean",
  permutations = 9999
)
adonis_Sinistral
```
Shape variation of sinistral elements among regions differs significantly. However disparity test shows significant differences to (see Exploratory data analysis - informative PCs - Region - Sinistral), therefore, differences between regions reflect both variation in average shape configuration and differences in the range of shape variability

#### Dextral
```{r}
set.seed(42)
adonis_Dextral <- adonis2(
  PC_scores[specimen_info_matched$Chirality == "Dextral", ] ~ Region,
  data = data_combined[specimen_info_matched$Chirality == "Dextral", ],
  method = "euclidean",
  permutations = 9999
)

adonis_Dextral

```
Shape variation of dextral elements among regions differs significantly. Disparity test shows no significant differences between region (see Exploratory data analysis - informative PCs - Region - Sinistral), therefore, differences between regions reflect average shape configuration.

#### Compare Chiralities within NE region
```{r}
set.seed(42)
adonis_Region_NE <- adonis2(
  PC_scores[specimen_info_matched$Region == "North-Eastern", ] ~ Chirality,
  data = data_combined[specimen_info_matched$Region == "North-Eastern", ],
  method = "euclidean",
  permutations = 9999
)

adonis_Region_NE

```

#### Compare Chiralities within W region
```{r}
set.seed(42)
adonis_Region_W <- adonis2(
  PC_scores[specimen_info_matched$Region == "Western", ] ~ Chirality,
  data = data_combined[specimen_info_matched$Region == "Western", ],
  method = "euclidean",
  permutations = 9999
)

adonis_Region_W

```


### Section
#### Sinistral
```{r}
set.seed(42)
# The number of analysed sinistral elements differed between section, and resampling method was employed

run_Section_test <- function(df, n_sample = 10){
  
  replicate(500, {
    
    keep <- unlist(
      lapply(levels(df$Section), function(sec){
        
        idx <- which(df$Section == sec)
        
        if(length(idx) > n_sample){
          sample(idx, n_sample)
        } else {
          idx
        }
        
      })
    )
    
    test <- adonis2(
      dist(df[keep, paste0("PC",1:7)]) ~ Section,
      data = df[keep, ],
      permutations = 999
    )
    
    test$`Pr(>F)`[1]
    
  })
}


results_sin_section <- run_Section_test(sin_data)

mean(results_sin_section < 0.05)

# pairwise_Sinistral
run_Section_pairwisetest_sin <- function(df, n_sample = 10, n_iter = 500){
  
  replicate(n_iter, {
    
    keep <- unlist(
      lapply(levels(df$Section), function(sec){
        
        idx <- which(df$Section == sec)
        
        if(length(idx) > n_sample){
          sample(idx, n_sample)
        } else {
          idx
        }
        
      })
    )
    
    pw <- pairwise.adonis2(
      dist(df[keep, paste0("PC",1:6)]) ~ Section,
      data = df[keep, ],
      permutations = 999
    )
    
    ## Extract the p-value from every comparison
    sapply(pw[-1], function(x) x$`Pr(>F)`[1])
    
  }, simplify = "matrix")
}
results_sin <- run_Section_pairwisetest_sin(sin_data)

rowMeans(results_sin)
rowMeans(results_sin < 0.05)

```
Sinistral elements significantly differ in shape among sections. To evaluate whether the differences in morphological variability were associated with unequal sam-ple size among sections, in 500 iterations, specimens were randomly subsampled within each section (10 samples per section) and differences in multivariate dispersion and average shape configuration were reassessed. 

A resampling approach showed the differences of multivariate shape between section is present in low % of 500 iteration. Therefore, differences in average shape configuration, when considering sample size, are not significant between sections. 


#### Dextral
```{r}
set.seed(42)

# The number of analysed dextral elements differed between section, and resampling method was employed

run_Section_test_dex <- function(df, n_sample = 8){
  
  replicate(500, {
    
    keep <- unlist(
      lapply(levels(df$Section), function(sec){
        
        idx <- which(df$Section == sec)
        
        if(length(idx) > n_sample){
          sample(idx, n_sample)
        } else {
          idx
        }
        
      })
    )
    
    test <- adonis2(
      dist(df[keep, paste0("PC",1:7)]) ~ Section,
      data = df[keep, ],
      permutations = 999
    )
    
    test$`Pr(>F)`[1]
    
  })
}


results_dex_section <- run_Section_test_dex(dex_data)

mean(results_dex_section < 0.05)

# pairwise
set.seed(42)
run_Section_pairwisetest_dex <- function(df, n_sample = 8, n_iter = 500){
  
  replicate(n_iter, {
    
    keep <- unlist(
      lapply(levels(df$Section), function(sec){
        
        idx <- which(df$Section == sec)
        
        if(length(idx) > n_sample){
          sample(idx, n_sample)
        } else {
          idx
        }
        
      })
    )
    
    pw <- pairwise.adonis2(
      dist(df[keep, paste0("PC",1:6)]) ~ Section,
      data = df[keep, ],
      permutations = 999
    )
    
    ## Extract the p-value from every comparison
    sapply(pw[-1], function(x) x$`Pr(>F)`[1])
    
  }, simplify = "matrix")
}
results_dex <- run_Section_pairwisetest_dex(dex_data)

rowMeans(results_dex)
rowMeans(results_dex < 0.05)

```
Dextral elements shape differs significantly among sections. However here to the sample size varies between section.

A resampling approach applied to PERMANOVA showed that differences of dextral elements in multivariate shape among sections remains significant in  high % of 500 iteration. Consequently, the observed differences among sections reflect average shape configuration. 

## Mean shape
### Chirality
```{r fig-chirality, fig.cap = "Mean shapes of Sinistral and Dextral elements"}
mean_shape_Sinistral <- geomorph::mshape(landmarks.gpa$coords[, , specimen_info_matched$Chirality == "Sinistral"])
mean_shape_Dextral <- geomorph::mshape(landmarks.gpa$coords[, , specimen_info_matched$Chirality == "Dextral"])



plot(
  mean_shape_Sinistral[,1],
  mean_shape_Sinistral[,2],
  asp = 1,
  type = "n",
  xlab = "X",
  ylab = "Y"
)
points(mean_shape_Sinistral[,1], mean_shape_Sinistral[,2],
       pch=21, bg="black")

points(mean_shape_Dextral[,1], mean_shape_Dextral[,2],
       pch=21, bg="grey")

legend(
  "topright",
  legend=c("Sinistral","Dextral"),
  pch=21,
  pt.bg=c("black","grey")
)
```

